course: dictionary
lesson: 12062
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You do not need to memorise every meaning. Read the sentence around the word, and the context tells you which meaning the writer means. «Classified» is one of these words.
explain: «The scientists classified the shells by their shape.» Here classified means sorted into groups. Check it by swapping in «sorted into groups»: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «The spy locked the classified plans in a safe.» Here classified means officially secret, only for certain people. The word «spy» and the locked safe are your clues. «Mum found a used bike in the classified ads.» Here classified means small advertisements in a newspaper or website, sorted into sections.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one to use.
fact: «Classified» can mean sorted into groups, as in «classified as mammals».
fact: «Classified» can mean officially secret, as in «classified information».
fact: «Classified ads» are small advertisements for things for sale or jobs.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The animals were classified as mammals.» What does classified mean here? | Small advertisements | *Sorted into groups | Hidden under the bed | Officially secret
exercise: «The agent kept the classified files in a locked drawer.» What does classified mean here? | Printed in the newspaper | Sorted into groups by colour | Old and broken | *Officially secret, only for certain people
exercise: Mum looked in the classified section for a new job. Which meaning fits? | *Small advertisements in a newspaper | Very quick | Secret | Sorted into groups
test: «The rocks were classified by colour.» What is the best meaning of classified? | *Sorted into groups | Cleaned | Secret | Hidden
test: Which phrase means information that is secret? | Classified as | *Classified information | Classified ads | Classified by size
exam: Which sentence uses classified to mean secret? | Lia read the classified ads for a puppy | *The spy hid the classified plans in her coat | The fish were classified by size
